-- title:
--   Restricted local fundamental class generates H²(H∩ D_w,K_w^×)
-- statement:
--   Let $E\subseteq K$ be number fields with $K/E$ Galois, let $w$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, and let $D_w$ denote [`NumberField.PlaceDecomp.decomp E K w`](def/NumberField_PlaceDecompositionAction.html#L82), the decomposition subgroup of $\mathrm{Gal}(K/E)=K\simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]}K$ attached to the valuation subring of $w$; assume $D_w$ is solvable. Fix a prime $q$ and a finite extension $L$ of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ inside a fixed algebraic closure, carrying compatible $D_w$-actions on $L$ and on $L^\times$, together with a ring isomorphism $\Phi : K_w \xrightarrow{\sim} L$ from the $w$-adic completion, subject to: $D_w$ fixes the image of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ in $L$, the unit action is induced by the field action, and $\Phi$ is $D_w$-equivariant. Let $K_0$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ which is a base for $L$ in the sense of [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.IsBase`](def/ExtCitation_LocalLevel_FundamentalClass.html#L13), i.e. $K_0\le L$ and an element of $L$ lies in $K_0$ exactly when it is fixed by all of $D_w$. Let $\theta$ be a morphism of $\mathbb{Z}$-linear $D_w$-representations from $L^\times$ (written additively) to $K_w^\times$ whose underlying map is $y\mapsto \Phi^{-1}(y)$, and let $u\in H^2(D_w,L^\times)$ satisfy [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.IsLocalFundamentalClass`](def/ExtCitation_LocalLevel_FundamentalClass.html#L60) for $(q,L,D_w,K_0)$: for every unramified overlay datum over $L$ with base $K_0$ — a finite extension $M\supseteq L$, a finite group $H$ acting faithfully on $M$, normal subgroups $N_L,N_n\le H$, an isomorphism $D_w\simeq H/N_L$, a Frobenius lift $\varphi$ and a uniformiser $\pi$ — together with a compatible embedding $\iota$ of $L^\times$ into $M^\times$, the pullback of $u$ equals the inflation of the class of the explicit carry $2$-cocycle built from $\varphi$ and $\pi$. Finally let $H\le \mathrm{Gal}(K/E)$ be any subgroup and put $S:=H\cap D_w$, with restriction taken along the inclusion $S\le D_w$. Then, writing $c$ for the image of $u$ in $H^2(S,K_w^\times)$ obtained by pushing $u$ forward along $\theta$ (the map induced by the identity of $D_w$ and $\theta$) and then restricting to $S$ (the map induced by the inclusion $S\le D_w$ and the identity of the restricted representation), the theorem asserts both that every $z\in H^2(S,K_w^\times)$ equals $m\cdot c$ for some $m\in\mathbb{Z}$, and that $m\cdot c=0$ if and only if $\#S$ divides $m$.
--
--   This is the local class-formation statement at a subgroup of the decomposition group: $H^2(S,K_w^\times)$ is cyclic of order $\#S$, generated by the restriction of the local fundamental class transported from $L^\times$ to $K_w^\times$. It is the version indexed by the inclusion $H\cap D_w\le D_w$, and is used in the Herbrand-quotient computation [`M4aHerbrand.finsum_div_natCard_decomp_cores_eq_finsum_div_natCard_inf_decomp`](thm.html#M4aHerbrand.finsum_div_natCard_decomp_cores_eq_finsum_div_natCard_inf_decomp) to read the summands of a double-coset decomposition as integers against one fundamental class per place.
